  "body": "Currently soft-logout (https://matrix.org/docs/spec/client_server/r0.6.1#soft-logout) defaults to `false` on 401 errors, for backwards compatibility.  This means that if someone accidentally puts their matrix CS API behind HTTP auth (as presumably per https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=27907696), then clients may see the 401 and hard logout, destroying local user data.  Instead, I suggest they should only explicitly hard logout if `soft-logout: false`.  (Alternatively, `hard-logout: true`).",
